{ignore}
<p><code>{themes/}</code> writes a switcher of the themes of <code>pad/subs/themes/types/</code>:
a list of them, with Default first, and a button. The form posts the choice back to the page,
which keeps it in a cookie of the application - its pages are in that theme from then on, this
one already: the pages built on the frame, or all of them when the application sets a
<code>$padTheme</code>; another application's never. Default takes the choice away: the
application's <code>$padTheme</code>, or the frame's own colours.</p>

<p>No script: the page changes when the visitor presses the button, not while an arrow key walks
the list, and it works without JavaScript. The form writes no token of its own, so showing it
or choosing starts no session, and a post from another site changes nothing; with
<code>$padCsrf</code> on it carries the session's token as every form then does.
<code>$padTheme = FALSE</code> turns themes off, the visitor's choice too.</p>
{/ignore}
